            <ArticleTitle>Pain: nocistatin spells relief.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>R525-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tissue or nerve injury can dramatically alter the transmission of sensory stimuli by spinal cord neurons, so that a light touch produces pain. The discovery that peptide products of prepronociceptin processing either facilitate or inhibit these mechanisms suggests novel approaches to treating these conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
